  "text": "proprium.sancti-laurentii-martyris-epistola",
  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Saint Lawrence, Martyr” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: Whoever sows sparingly will reap sparingly as well, and whoever sows in blessings will reap from blessings as well. Each one should give as he has resolved in his heart, not out of sadness or out of necessity; for God loves a cheerful giver. And God has the power to make every grace abound in you, so that, in all things always having all sufficiency, you may abound for every good work, as it is written: “He scattered, he gave to the poor; his justice endures forever and ever.” And He who supplies seed to the sower will also provide bread to eat, and will multiply your seed, and will add to the increase of the fruits of your justice." }
  },
